  <data name="S_WindowsDefaultSleepModernStandby.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Windows' default Sleep (Modern Standby) sometimes drains the battery from background wake-ups or fails to resume cleanly. Hibernate saves the session to disk and fully powers off, which is closer to how SteamOS suspends and tends to be more reliable - at the cost of a slightly slower resume. Setting the Power Button and Hibernate Timeout options above to Hibernate (and disabling Windows' Sleep timer) is the recommended change.</value></data>
